484	    // A fill into a line that is already resident (a sector refill) must target
485	    // the resident way, not a fresh victim, so the new sector lands in the same
486	    // line copy. With 1 sector/line a fill's line is never already resident, so
487	    // this is gated off and the victim way is always used (legacy behavior).
